solution.p:
Parallel lines have the same slope, and the slope of y=17.2x-340.9 is 17.2\text{.} So \ell has slope 17.2\text{.} And we have been given that \ells y-intercept is at (0,128.2)\text{.} So we can use slope-intercept form to write its equation as
y=17.2x+128.2
            \text{.}

