###### # Body ######
BEGIN_PGML A line [`\ell`] is parallel to the line with equation [`y=17.2x-340.9\text{,}`] but [`\ell`] has [`y`]-intercept at [`(0,128.2)\text{.}`] What is an equation for [`\ell\text{?}`]
[_]{$line}{20}
END_PGML
########## # Solution ##########
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION Parallel lines have the same slope, and the slope of [`y=17.2x-340.9`] is [`17.2\text{.}`] So [`\ell`] has slope [`17.2\text{.}`] And we have been given that [`\ell`]'s [`y`]-intercept is at [`(0,128.2)\text{.}`] So we can use slope-intercept form to write its equation as
[``` y=17.2x+128.2 \text{.}```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
############# # End Problem #############
ENDDOCUMENT();
